+
+## Forward V20: one owner-authorized terminal retirement batch
+
+The new closed laboratory package adds one bounded optional wire on the
+existing trusted package anchor. The owned scope-zero fixture can install
+one exact batch only from the committed open position 3. It takes the
+package lock, both pinned writer binding locks and the scope head lock.
+It verifies the intact independently held catalog, exact role identities,
+unchanged package and prepared original Stop. In that one fixture
+transaction it records the original Stop Command digest and the exact
+installer and recorder identities and removes LOGIN from those two roles.
+It creates no worker administration endpoint or grant.
+
+When the marker is present, authentication checks that terminal boundary
+before raw catalog equality. It independently resolves both selected
+writers from finalized scoped Install and Acquire and the held canonical
+bindings. Each exact writer name and OID must still have NOLOGIN. A
+transient full-catalog comparison changes only those two login bits and
+requires the original V20 digest. Any additional catalog or role drift
+refuses. Restoring both login bits while leaving the marker present also
+refuses. V19 behavior remains the marker-absent path.
+
+The actual live control may submit the exact reserved Stop at position
+4 only. The package row is held through deferred COMMIT, which checks the
+same marker, exact command digest, actor and catalog. Its one historical
+dependency read is restricted to the exact committed Resume at 3 and
+receives only private terminal context. All other mutation and submit
+replay paths stay closed while the marker exists. The actual live reader
+may retrieve exact committed originals written by the two pinned writers
+and the exact committed Stop, with the normal independent historical
+assembly. Unknown, nonreader, wrong-original and provisional requests
+cannot use terminal recovery.
+
+The one focused native case checks a trusted lock refusal, actor and
+sealed-owner marker DML denial, atomic owner issuance, exact independent
+readback for both writer originals, denial of unrelated scope and catalog
+state, late unrelated drift refusal at COMMIT and exact reserved Stop
+readback. All 39 previously retained methods are byte-identical. Fixture
+teardown alone restores the synthetic role bits and marker. The extra
+bounded anchor update is separate from the actor row/key ledger.
+
+V20 is a fresh private source and catalog seal, not an installed V19
+migration. A separate native run and independent review remain required.
+The package catalog still spans fixture scopes, so the second fixture
+scope fails closed while scope zero is retired. The trusted procedure is
+bounded to its owned test database and does not establish protection from
+out-of-band privileged DDL, cross-package archive recovery or production
+retirement authority.
